WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.660
You’re a member of an elite Mobile Task
Force, tracking down an anomaly in a rural

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:10.330
village somewhere in the Swiss Alps that was
recently detected by SCP Foundation Field

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.330
Agents.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.960
According to all the current intel, you’re
dealing with a particularly deadly and hard-to-contain

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:21.940
monster: A shapeshifting entity that can kill
with a touch, and assume the form of anyone

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.020
it kills.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.400
If this thing somehow escaped the village
and broke into a major population center,

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.030
it could blend in perfectly and cause death
on a massive scale.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:35.710
It’s up to you and your team to get this
creature secured and contained before that

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:36.710
can happen.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.690
You’re going in heavily armed, with advanced
sensory technology and several attack helicopters,

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.620
each one loaded with plenty of powerful missiles.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.410
One way or another, you’re putting a stop
to this thing.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:54.500
But the best laid plans of Mobile Task Force
agents go often awry.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:59.290
The mission is a bloodbath - the shapeshifting
anomaly has blended in perfectly with the

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.120
innocent civilians living in the village.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.920
Before you know it, half of your team have
been killed, and you don’t know which of

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.540
the remaining team members are really themselves.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.940
This really couldn’t have gone worse, and
if you mess this up, not only is your life

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:19.520
at risk, but so are the lives of everyone
this anomaly happens to get close to.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.100
All of your superiors were killed or transformed
in the battle with the shapeshifter, and you’re

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.490
now sitting at the top of your MTF’s chain
of command.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.480
The way you see it, there’s only one option.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.120
You radio up to air support, alerting the
several attack choppers circling the village.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.090
You tell them to rain fire and destroy the
whole place; that’s the only way to be sure

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.090
to take out the anomaly.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.770
Things have gone beyond the point of easy
containment.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:50.230
You sprint past the village limits as a volley
of missiles and firebombs raze the formerly-quiet

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.750
settlement to the ground.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:56.340
Other than the Task Force members in the helicopters,
you’re the only survivor.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.710
Over 320 people are dead.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:03.820
But on the upside, the remains of the shapeshifting
anomaly were found amongst the rubble by Foundation

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.030
personnel.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:09.750
You prevented whatever horrors it would have
caused if it had been allowed to escape.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.760
Mission accomplished.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.340
But it’s not over yet.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:17.360
When you solemnly return to the Containment
Site you’d been deployed from, your superiors

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.350
order you to go pay a visit to Conference
Room 2.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.980
You correctly assume that it’s some kind
of disciplinary meeting - maybe the Site Director

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.870
chewing you out for shoddy work, but ultimately
congratulating you for doing what needed to

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.670
be done under pressure.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:37.090
After all, making the tough decisions is what
working for the SCP Foundation is all about.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:41.430
But when you arrive in the Conference Room,
you’re sitting across from a woman you’ve

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.730
never seen before.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:48.280
She’s tall, with hard, stern-looking features,
and a plain but well-tailored suit.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.590
Despite being a hardened soldier on the Foundation
payroll, something about this woman makes

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:53.590
you nervous.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.200
She smiles, and says:

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.310
“Hello, I’m with the Foundation Ethics
Committee.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.830
We need to have a word.”

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.640
For reasons you don’t quite understand,
you start to break into a cold sweat.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.640
The Ethics Committee?

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.990
I thought they existed just to scare Foundation
employees.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.240
I didn’t know they had actual authority.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.390
But that’s where you made a terrible mistake.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.770
And from the tight smile on the agent’s
face, you can tell that the Foundation Ethics

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.739
Committee has a lot more power than you’ve
ever imagined.

00:03:19.739 --> 00:03:23.690
Perhaps you know them from the jokes that
float around Foundation circles - “How many

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.530
members of the Ethics Committee does it take
to change a lightbulb?

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.530
None!

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.290
The Ethics Committee can't change anything!”

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.930
Perhaps you’ve heard about the O5 Council’s
disdain for them, those bureaucratic pencil-pushers

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.800
with all their rubber stamps and red tape.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.620
The jokes don’t seem so funny now though.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.140
The Ethics Committee representative clears
her throat, and tells you that you’re being

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.410
reassigned, effective immediately.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:52.180
You’re now under the employ of the Foundation
Ethics Committee, and this change is non-negotiable.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.510
You try to state your case in a blind panic.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:58.370
Part of you thinks being “reassigned to
the Ethics Committee'' after the mistake you

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:03.920
just made is code for “being taken into
a windowless room and shot in the back of

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.920
your head.”

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.390
But the agent insists that really isn’t
the case - the Ethics Committee hates codes

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.390
and euphemisms.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.410
They don’t say “terminated”, they say
“killed.”

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.549
Because at the Ethics Committee, clarity of
language is extremely important.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:22.479
They don’t sanitize any horrific acts that
need to be performed for the sake of containment

00:04:22.479 --> 00:04:27.790
- After all, it’s their job to look these
horrors in the face, and give the final “Yes''

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.460
or “No” on whether they’re carried out.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:35.300
As you may know, the SCP Foundation is essentially
above all external law.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:40.550
No government, no organization, and no individual
can tell them what to do.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.800
The thirteen members of the O5 Council have
almost unlimited knowledge at their disposal,

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.120
as well as technology that the rest of the
world could only ever dream of.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:55.029
With a setup like that, it would be easy to
give into corruption and go mad with power.

00:04:55.029 --> 00:04:59.840
If they wanted to, they could abandon their
mission of protecting humanity from the shadows,

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.910
and instead rule the world with an iron fist.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.180
That’s where the all-important role of the
Foundation Ethics Committee comes in.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:12.080
As Uncle Ben once said, “with great power
comes great responsibility.”

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:17.210
Just as the O5 Council wields the power, the
Ethics Committee wields the responsibility.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:22.770
They remind the whole organization that they
are here to serve the world, not the other

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.000
way around.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.860
Think of them as the conscience of the SCP
Foundation - they decide what’s morally

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:34.300
acceptable for the Foundation to do in pursuit
of its goals, to make sure that those who

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.809
fight monsters don’t become monsters themselves.

00:05:37.809 --> 00:05:44.490
As Nietzsche famously said, “if you gaze
long into an abyss, the abyss also gazes into

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:45.490
you.”

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:49.610
Right now, you very much feel like you’re
staring into the abyss, as the Ethics Committee

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:53.099
representative calmly explains the situation
to you.

00:05:53.099 --> 00:05:57.969
An important thing to remember about the Foundation
is that it must be cold, not cruel.

00:05:57.969 --> 00:06:02.409
The second that the harm it causes is in excess
of the positive results of the Foundation’s

00:06:02.409 --> 00:06:07.400
actions, it’s time for the Ethics Committee
to step in and dole out some discipline.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:12.149
It is the Ethics Committee’s job to balance
the moral cost of every action performed by

00:06:12.149 --> 00:06:16.610
the Foundation - from the degree of collateral
damage permissible in the field, to the ways

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:20.349
that D-Classes can be ethically used in testing.

00:06:20.349 --> 00:06:24.360
While some hardcore Foundation loyalists may
say that people like the Ethics Committee

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.889
are standing in the way of true progress,
giving yourself wholly to the mission without

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:32.309
any ethical safeguards can be a dangerous
line to walk.

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:37.259
At that point, what’s separating the Foundation
from the Global Occult Coalition or the Chaos

00:06:37.259 --> 00:06:38.449
Insurgency?

00:06:38.449 --> 00:06:44.330
Or even worse, their nightmarish alternate
selves from the universes of SCP-1730 and

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:45.330
SCP-5000?

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.469
While the Foundation occasionally needs to
do some truly horrific things in order to

00:06:50.469 --> 00:06:56.150
Secure, Contain, and Protect, it’s the Ethics
Committee that keeps them on the moral high

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.150
ground.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:01.610
All of this seems pretty complicated to you,
as you sit, still fearing for your life in

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.009
Conference Room 2.

00:07:03.009 --> 00:07:07.639
The Ethics Committee agent explains that it’s
actually all quite simple, once you get used

00:07:07.639 --> 00:07:08.639
to it.

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:12.789
The Ethics Committee uses a moral framework
known as Utilitarianism - Think of it like

00:07:12.789 --> 00:07:15.189
the product of morality and math.

00:07:15.189 --> 00:07:20.529
Specifically, the Committee uses an ethical
system known as Negative Utilitarianism.

00:07:20.529 --> 00:07:24.740
This system revolves around the principle
of “Harm Reduction” - the Committee tries

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:30.929
to modify every action taken to cause the
least amount of possible suffering in a situation.

00:07:30.929 --> 00:07:34.819
The goal being to eliminate any unnecessary
suffering from an action.

00:07:34.819 --> 00:07:39.259
“Take your decision, for example,” the
Ethics Committee representative says.

00:07:39.259 --> 00:07:43.909
“Your actions - namely, the destruction
of the village - caused a great deal of suffering.

00:07:43.909 --> 00:07:47.870
However, considering the damage the anomaly
could have caused after your team lost control

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:51.889
of the situation, it’s clear that your motivation
was ultimately pure harm-reduction.

00:07:51.889 --> 00:07:56.099
I admire that kind of thinking in a high-pressure
situation.”

00:07:56.099 --> 00:07:59.209
You feel a cool wave of relief wash over you.

00:07:59.209 --> 00:08:03.310
It feels safe to assume at this point that
this probably isn’t just a big front for

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.349
your immediate termination.

00:08:05.349 --> 00:08:09.330
The agent sitting across from you seems to
sense that that’s what you’re thinking,

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:12.069
and assures you that she’s being nothing
but honest with you.

00:08:12.069 --> 00:08:17.449
The Ethics Committee has no need to be petty
- They know everything, after all.

00:08:17.449 --> 00:08:23.369
And that’s not an exaggeration - Their clearance
is basically the equivalent to Level 5, the

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.650
highest in the Foundation.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:30.749
Every line ever redacted from an SCP Foundation
file, they were privy to.

00:08:30.749 --> 00:08:35.250
Every secret the Foundation has ever kept,
they have absolute access to.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.890
And every decision the Foundation has ever
made?

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:44.990
The Ethics Committee has always had the final
say - with veto power even over the O5 Council.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:49.490
And most importantly, all members of the Ethics
Committee are former Foundation personnel

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:53.970
- Site Directors, Researchers, Mobile Task
Force operatives.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:57.390
All people whose decisions have caused pain
and death.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:02.430
Much like jury duty, the responsibility is
random and non-negotiable.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:06.440
What you’re experiencing right now isn’t
a normal disciplinary hearing - it’s an

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.770
employee orientation.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:13.570
The cruel irony, for a department of the Foundation
devoted to ethical conduct, is that it’s

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:18.030
actually complicit in pretty much all of the
Foundation’s worst moral crimes.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:22.650
After all, every action that the Foundation
has ever performed has been performed with

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:26.440
the permission and cooperation of the Ethics
Committee.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:32.660
Take the infamous Procedure 110-Montauk, used
to prevent the victims of SCP-231 giving birth.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:37.520
The Ethics Committee had a key role in designing
the horrific procedure, and now, they have

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:43.360
to live with the soul-crushing knowledge of
exactly what that procedure entails.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.580
And soon, you will too.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.610
Just one of the many “perks” of joining
the committee.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:51.620
“It isn’t the easiest job,” the representative
tells you.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:56.100
She’s got the steely, blank eyes of someone
who’s seen some things that people were

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.820
never meant to see.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:02.790
She continues, “Before we conclude the first
part of your orientation, I suppose I should

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.540
tell you about the Sowing Circle.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.650
That’ll give you a good idea of what you’re
in for.”

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:12.880
She tells you that the Sowing Circle was the
anomaly discussed in the 2017 Ethics Committee

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:13.880
Roundtable.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:18.100
It’s an anomaly so secretive that it was
never given an official containment number

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:22.740
or classification, but it was proposed as
a solution to one of the Foundation’s most

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:26.860
nightmarish problems: The shortage of human
infants.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:31.910
It’s an ugly truth about the Foundation
that a decent number of anomalies - such as

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:38.160
SCP-2845, the Deer - require the sacrifice
of live children as part of their containment

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.160
procedures.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:43.540
For years, the Foundation had been stealing
children from orphanages for the use in these

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:49.320
rituals, but the Sowing Circle could solve
this problem: It was a mummified human corpse,

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:52.290
wreathed in a circle of its own dried-out
intestines.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:57.300
The mummy produced seeds which, if consumed,
could allow human women to produce litters

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:03.440
of twelve babies with an eight hour gestation
period, like the litters of a sow - hence

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.450
the name.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.140
This would solve the baby shortage handily.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.740
It was the job of the Ethics Committee to
decide what would be the most ethical way

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.750
to use this anomaly.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:17.830
In the end, despite their own personal, moral
disgust at the actions, their philosophy of

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:23.970
harm reduction led them to one conclusion:
Using the device to impregnate already brain-dead

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:29.500
patients, effectively turning them into comatose
infant factories whose only purpose was to

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.980
be used in horrific containment procedures.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:38.010
But ultimately, the sacrifice would pale compared
to the pain averted - seeing as millions,

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:43.290
if not billions, would be under threat from
some of these entities being released.

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:46.960
Not that this makes the knowledge of what
needs to be done any easier to handle on a

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.250
personal level.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:53.510
But of course, after what you did at the village,
you know this feeling all too well already.

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:58.860
The pain and the guilt you felt at making
that decision is going to follow you your

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.260
whole life.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:04.760
And now you’re about to have countless more
experiences piled on top.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:08.470
It’s your burden, your duty, your job.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:11.180
The Ethics Committee agent forces a weak smile.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:17.250
She says, “Of course, nobody said the job
was easy, but somebody needs to do it…”

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:23.120
Now check out “SCP-001 - The Scarlet King”
and “Secret Group that Runs the World - SCP

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:27.050
O5 Council Explained” for more SCP Foundation
deep lore!

